  "text": "That sounds like a wonderful idea! A classic breakfast omelette is a simple yet delicious way to show your mom you care. Here's a basic recipe for a classic omelette, along with some tips to make it extra special:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf73 **Classic Breakfast Omelette Recipe**\n\n**Ingredients:**\n- 2 large eggs\n- 1/4 cup milk (or water for a lighter version)\n- 1/2 teaspoon salt\n- 1/8 teaspoon pepper\n- 1 tablespoon butter (or oil, for a non-stick pan)\n- Optional: cheese (cheddar, Swiss, or any favorite type), vegetables (like spinach, mushrooms, or diced tomatoes), or cooked meat (like ham or bacon)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. **Whisk the eggs:** In a bowl, beat the eggs with a fork or whisk. Add the milk, salt, and pepper. Mix well.\n\n2. **Heat the pan:** Place a non-stick skillet over medium heat. Add the butter or oil and let it melt.\n\n3. **Cook the eggs:** Pour the egg mixture into the pan. Let it cook for 1-2 minutes until the edges start to set.\n\n4. **Add fillings (optional):** If you're using cheese, vegetables, or meat, add them to the omelette now. Fold one side of the omelette over the other and cook for another minute or two.\n\n5. **Flip and finish:** If you want a perfectly cooked omelette, you can carefully flip it with a spatula and cook for another 1-2 minutes, or use the \"sliding\" technique by gently lifting the edges and letting the uncooked parts cook.\n\n6. **Serve:** Slide the omelette onto a plate and serve warm.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 **Tips for Success:**\n- Use a non-stick pan to prevent sticking.\n- Don\u2019t overcook the omelette; it should be soft and fluffy on the inside.\n- Experiment with fillings to make it your own\u2014like adding some fresh herbs (basil, parsley), a bit of cream cheese, or even a sprinkle of paprika.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf81 **To Make It a Surprise:**\n- Presentation is key! Serve it on a small plate with a side of toast or fruit.\n- Add a little ribbon or flower as a garnish for a touch of elegance.\n- Leave a note or make a small card to go along with it to make it even more special.\n\n---\n\nLet me know if you'd like a version with specific fillings or dietary adaptations (like vegan or gluten-free), and I'd be happy to help! You're doing a great thing by making your mom breakfast in bed \u2014 it\u2019s a thoughtful and delicious way to celebrate her! \ud83c\udf89\u2764\ufe0f",
